      "text": "Given that four positive integers \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), and \\(D\\) sum to 36 and they satisfy the equations \\(A+2 = B-2 = C \\times 2 = D \\div 2 = k\\) for some constant \\(k\\), we can express each variable in terms of \\(k\\):\n\n\\[\nA = k - 2, \\quad B = k + 2, \\quad C = \\frac{k}{2}, \\quad D = 2k\n\\]\n\nWe know that the sum of these integers is 36:\n\n\\[\nA + B + C + D = 36\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the expressions for \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), and \\(D\\) in terms of \\(k\\):\n\n\\[\n(k - 2) + (k + 2) + \\frac{k}{2} + 2k = 36\n\\]\n\nSimplify the left-hand side:\n\n\\[\nk - 2 + k + 2 + \\frac{k}{2} + 2k = 36\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\n4k + \\frac{k}{2} = 36\n\\]\n\nTo eliminate the fraction, multiply every term by 2:\n\n\\[\n8k + k = 72\n\\]\n\n\\[\n9k = 72\n\\]\n\nSolve for \\(k\\):\n\n\\[\nk = \\frac{72}{9} = 8\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\(k = 8\\) back into the expressions for \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), and \\(D\\):\n\n\\[\nA = k - 2 = 8 - 2 = 6\n\\]\n\\[\nB = k + 2 = 8 + 2 = 10\n\\]\n\\[\nC = \\frac{k}{2} = \\frac{8}{2} = 4\n\\]\n\\[\nD = 2k = 2 \\times 8 = 16\n\\]\n\nFinally, calculate the product \\(A \\times B \\times C \\times D\\):\n\n\\[\nA \\times B \\times C \\times D = 6 \\times 10 \\times 4 \\times 16\n\\]\n\nFirst, multiply \\(6\\) and \\(10\\):\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nNext, multiply the result by \\(4\\):\n\n\\[\n60 \\times 4 = 240\n\\]\n\nFinally, multiply the result by \\(16\\):\n\n\\[\n240 \\times 16 = 240 \\times (10 + 6) = 240 \\times 10 + 240 \\times 6 = 2400 + 1440 = 3840\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the product \\(A \\times B \\times C \\times D\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3840}\n\\]",
